      "content": "Good choices to be mindful of! You'll want to avoid foods like white rice, sugary cereals, and white bread, as they are high GI. For a low GI swap, consider brown rice or quinoa instead of white rice. If you're craving a sweet treat, swap sugary pastries for an apple or berries, which are much lower on the GI scale. These substitutions can make meal planning much easier for managing blood sugar.",
